# Project Structure for Anthropic Computer Use Tools

This is a Tauri v2 application that implements Anthropic Computer Use functionality, allowing Claude to interact with a computer's desktop environment.

## Key Components

- **Main Application**
  - [src-tauri/src/lib.rs](mdc:dotdot/src-tauri/src/lib.rs) - Core application initialization and Tauri setup
  - [src-tauri/src/commands/](mdc:dotdot/src-tauri/src/commands) - Tauri commands for user interface to backend communication

- **Computer Use SDK**
  - [src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/](mdc:dotdot/src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level) - Core SDK implementation for desktop automation
  - [src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/platforms/](mdc:dotdot/src-tauri/mcp-server-os-level/src/platforms) - Platform-specific implementations (macOS, Windows, Linux)

- **Testing Framework**
  - [test-rust-units.sh](mdc:dotdot/test-rust-units.sh) - Runs Rust unit tests with verbose output
  - [run-tests.sh](mdc:dotdot/run-tests.sh) - Main test runner script for basic tests
  - [test-qa.sh](mdc:dotdot/test-qa.sh) - QA testing for user interface automation features
  - [qa-test-plan.md](mdc:dotdot/qa-test-plan.md) - Comprehensive test plan for the project

- **Frontend Implementation**
  - [src/](mdc:dotdot/src) - React frontend implementation
  - [src/components/](mdc:dotdot/src/components) - UI components including DevToolsPanel for testing

The application follows a layered architecture with clear separation between UI commands, core functionality in the SDK, and platform-specific implementations. Each platform implementation (macOS, Windows, Linux) is separated within the SDK.
